      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Cache nodes replace fluid pipes entirely. A Steam Cache Node is a 16,000,000 L digital tank that auto-outputs 2,000,000 L/s through the face it points at; the Reinforced grade quadruples to 64,000,000 L and 8,000,000 L/s and binds to hubs for two-way transfer at the same rate.\n\nThe upgrade path is crafting-table cheap: triple bronze plates and large bronze pipes around a ULV fluid tank core, then triple steel around your existing node. Binding costs 0 singularities plain, 1 reinforced — the friendliest bill in the family.\n\nThen build the void reservoir, the old dream: a Water Hub Array with fluid cache nodes capped over your water works — nodes of 2M / 8M / 32M liters interacting at 64K-2M per cycle, all binding for zero singularities. The tank farm retires, and the boilers never calcify on distilled again.",
